-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/200e6dc7-10a7-539e-a7d9-f349128432ba
-- title:
--   Level-independence of chart preimages of an open of X
-- statement:
--   The statement is set in the framework of a Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation datum; the hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   **Base ring.** A prime $r$; a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an element $\pi$ of $\mathcal{O}$ that is irreducible (`hπ`), with $\mathcal{O}$ complete for the $\pi$-adic topology (`hcomplete`), residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`), and $r$ and $\pi$ generating the same ideal of $\mathcal{O}$ (`hunr`, absolute unramifiedness); a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra and a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **Unramified extension.** A characteristic-zero domain $O^{nr}$ with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $F_r$, subject to: $O^{nr}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`); that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`); every $x \in O^{nr}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`); every monic polynomial over $O^{nr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`); and $F_r x \equiv x^{r}$ modulo $\pi$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **Determinant valuation.** A monoid homomorphism $v_{\det} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) such that $v_{\det}(g) = n$ holds exactly when $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal{O}$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Group data.** A group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, a subgroup $\Gamma \le G$ containing an element $z$ with $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix and $v_{\det}(\sigma z) = 2$ (`hcent`) and an element $w$ with $v_{\det}(\sigma w) = 1$ (`hodd`), and a subgroup $\Gamma'$ whose elements are precisely the $x \in \Gamma$ with $v_{\det}(\sigma x)$ even (`hΓ'`). Furthermore a homomorphism $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ which is the projectivisation of $\sigma$ pointwise (`hρ`), such that the image $\rho(\Gamma')$ acts on the vertices of the lattice tree [`LT.LatticeTree.Vertex 𝒪 K₀`](def/LatticeTreeOrbital.html#L349) (homothety classes of full $\mathcal{O}$-lattices in $K_0^2$) with finite vertex stabilisers (`hdisc`) and with finitely many orbits, witnessed by a finite set of vertices meeting every orbit (`hcocpt`).
--
--   **The scheme.** A scheme $\mathcal{X}$ together with a proper flat morphism $f : \mathcal{X} \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **The uniformisation map $\Theta$.** For each $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map $\Theta$ from the set of pairs $(\psi, P)$, with $\psi : O^{nr} \to B$ an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism and $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$ (a family of $B$-submodules $P.\mathrm{line}\,M \subseteq B \otimes_{\mathcal{O}} M$, indexed by the full $\mathcal{O}$-lattices $M \subseteq K_0^2$, with invertible quotients, compatible with inclusions of lattices and with homotheties, and non-degenerate at every prime of $B$), to the set of $B$-points of $f$, i.e. pairs consisting of a morphism $\operatorname{Spec}B \to \mathcal{X}$ whose composite with $f$ is the structure morphism $\operatorname{Spec}B \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$. The four hypotheses on $\Theta$ are: naturality in $B$ along $\mathcal{O}$-algebra maps (`hΘnat`); invariance under the twisted $\Gamma$-action, that is $\Theta(x') = \Theta(x)$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma$ and `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` holds for $\sigma\gamma$ and the pair $x, x'$, namely $x'_1 = x_1 \circ F_r^{-v_{\det}(\sigma\gamma)}$ and $x'_2.\mathrm{line}\,M$ is the preimage of $x_2.\mathrm{line}\,((\sigma\gamma)^{-1}M)$ under the base-changed action map, for every full lattice $M$ (`hΘinv`); for every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent and every $\psi : O^{nr} \to k$, that $\Theta(\psi, \cdot)$ is surjective onto the $k$-points of $f$ and that $\Theta(\psi,P) = \Theta(\psi,P')$ holds exactly when $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ are related by the twisted action of some $\gamma \in \Gamma$ (`hΘfib`); and universality (`hΘuniv`): for every scheme $T$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ and every family $\rho'$ of maps into the $B$-points of $T$ that is natural in $B$ and invariant under the twisted $\Gamma$-action, there is a family $u$ of maps from the $B$-points of $f$ to the $B$-points of $T$, natural in $B$, with $u \circ \Theta = \rho'$, and any other natural family with this property agrees with $u$ on all $B$ and all points.
--
--   **Chart data.** The element $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi, 1)$ (`hg₁`); for each $n$, the morphism $s_n : \operatorname{Spec}(O^{nr}/\pi^{n+1}) \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$, equal to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map (`hsn`); and, for each $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and each $n$, a morphism
--   $$\kappa_{h,n} : \operatorname{Spec}\bigl(A/\pi^{n+1}A\bigr) \longrightarrow \mathcal{X} \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}} \operatorname{Spec}(O^{nr}/\pi^{n+1}),$$
--   where $A =$ `chartERing Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) r` is the localisation of the quotient of $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, O^{nr})$ by the ideal generated by `edgeRel` at the powers of the element `edgeQuot.discr`, and the target is the pullback of $f$ along $s_n$. These morphisms satisfy the chart law `hκ`: for all $h$, $n$, every commutative ring $B$ that is simultaneously an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra and an $O^{nr}$-algebra compatibly, with the image of $\pi$ nilpotent, every $O^{nr}$-algebra homomorphism $\bar{x} : A/\pi^{n+1}A \to B$ and all Deligne data $d, P$ over $B$: if the line of $d$ at the standard full lattice is the $B$-span of $\bar{x}(\xi)\otimes e_0 + 1 \otimes e_1$, the line of $d$ at the $g_1$-translate of the standard lattice is the image under the base-changed action map of the $B$-span of $1 \otimes e_0 + \bar{x}(\eta)\otimes e_1$ (with $\xi =$ `chartERing.ξ` and $\eta =$ `chartERing.η` the two distinguished elements of $A$, taken modulo $\pi^{n+1}$), and $d$ lies in the edge chart for the pair $(g_1 \cdot \mathrm{std}, \mathrm{std})$, i.e. the edge non-degeneracy conditions hold at every prime of $B$, and moreover $P$ is the pullback of $d$ along $h^{-1}$, then the morphism $\operatorname{Spec}B \to \mathcal{X}$ underlying $\Theta_B(\mathrm{struct}_{O^{nr}\to B}, P)$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\bar{x})$ followed by $\kappa_{h,n}$ followed by the first projection of the pullback of $f$ along $s_n$.
--
--   **Data of the assertion.** An open subset $V$ of $\mathcal{X}$, an element $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, an element $t \in A$, and a natural number $n$; the hypothesis `ht₀` states that the basic open subset of $\operatorname{Spec}(A/\pi^{0+1}A)$ determined by the class of $t$ is contained in the preimage under $\kappa_{h,0}$ of the preimage under the first projection $\mathcal{X} \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}} \operatorname{Spec}(O^{nr}/\pi)\to\mathcal{X}$ of $V$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** The basic open subset of $\operatorname{Spec}(A/\pi^{n+1}A)$ determined by the class of $t$ is contained in the preimage under $\kappa_{h,n}$ of the preimage under the first projection of the pullback of $f$ along $s_n$ of the open set $V$.
--
--   The chart morphisms $\kappa_{h,n}$ at different levels $n$ have the same source topological space, $\pi$ being nilpotent in each $A/\pi^{n+1}A$, and this result says that whether a basic open of that space is carried into a given open $V$ of $\mathcal{X}$ does not depend on the level. It is used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_finset_chartUnitLocus_cover_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_finset_chartUnitLocus_cover_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient), where finitely many chart basic opens are chosen to cover the special fibre simultaneously at all levels.
